  "hypothesis": "Screening unsustainable fully visible sleeping camp pulls in both targeting and routing increases matched wins over the edit base without new faults or fuel suspensions. Nonpositive matched win gain or new reliability failures falsify it.",
  "mechanism_status": "Unmeasured rules/source deduction; final aggregates show camp mortality but do not prove unsafe initial pulls caused the losses.",
  "bottleneck": "Nearest camp attacks can awaken a group without considering its remaining HP, damage or nearby support.",
  "policy": "Assess at most six fully visible sleeping groups (32 visible camps maximum), estimate 0.6 * summed camp strength * ceil(remaining HP / nearby basic DPS), and defer fresh pulls above 80% of current nearby allied health. Include healthy visible allies within four tiles. Apply same group exclusion to combat and camp travel; prevent camp-directed splash into excluded groups. If all eligible goals would disappear retain base behavior. Reassess after movement; no cached live state.",
  "alternatives": "Broader risk-priced routing/draft/commitment and predictive retreat were tried previously and remain separate negative findings. This changes only initiation of fully observed sleeping fights and adds no global scorer, new recovery trigger, draft, shopping, commitment or shared memory. Different from the earlier package because it preserves the successful current kit-aware build and all ongoing fights.",
  "expected_observable_change": "Fewer camp deaths and improved collection/tribute and matched wins. These are not yet measured.",
  "risk": "Conservative basic-only DPS may defer viable spell/splash fights; allied proximity does not guarantee participation; hiding a group removes the veto; fully-visible big groups may be rare.",
  "plan": [
    "Write and run a source invariant regression on base (expected RED).",
    "Implement bounded sleeping-group assessment and coupled combat/route exclusion with no new state.",
    "Run invariant check and trusted bot-check, inspect exact-source smoke summaries, review diff.",
    "Update compact notes and return one candidate."
  ],
